  "_comment": [
    "CLA-76's fitted static curve, 20 coarse stairs.wav captures at 96 kHz \u2014 the",
    "OUTPUT of `npm run fet:stairs`, kept because the captures are licensed audio.",
    "Companion to fetish_stairs_fits.json; same reasons, same caveats.",
    "",
    "\u26a0 THE KNEE COLUMN IS MOSTLY UNUSABLE AND IS KEPT ANYWAY. The instrument's own",
    "knee floor at attack dial 1 is 4.32 dB, so every reading at or under it is the",
    "fit leaving the parameterisation rather than a sharp knee measured. Values at",
    "exactly 0.50 sat on an older search bound. Read `kneeUnresolved` semantics in",
    "`fet-stairs.mjs`, not these numbers.",
    "",
    "\u26a0 THESE ARE ATTACK DIAL 1 (the old protocol). The gate bounce showed CLA-76 is",
    "attack-invariant on this test \u2014 slope moved 0.0057 and knee 0.24 sweeping the",
    "dial end to end \u2014 so they are not attack-biased, which is why they remain",
    "usable. Our own side of any comparison is biased at dial 1 and is not.",
    "",
    "\u26a0 CLA-76's THRESHOLD MOVES WITH THE RATIO BUTTON, by 4.5 dB end to end, and",
    "ours does not. That is a topology disagreement, not a number to average away."
